0..62 Comment "// A functor over a theory\'s models: a parameter written `(S :"
63..139 Comment "// Model(T))` takes the signature the theory `T` derives, its sorts abstract"
140..216 Comment "// in the body and its operations values at the types the theory states, and"
217..292 Comment "// an application matches its argument against that signature by name, so a"
293..367 Comment "// module ascribed the record signature the theory presents is an argument"
368..443 Comment "// as a model is. After Kaposi and Xie (_Second-Order Generalised Algebraic"
444..506 Comment "// Theories: Signatures and First-Order Semantics_, FSCD 2024,"
507..579 Comment "// doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10), under which a module signature is a"
580..646 Comment "// theory and a parameterised module the static half of a functor."
647..649 Comment "//"
650..665 Comment "// - see: #1226"
666..701 Comment "// - see: #1764 — `Reassociating`"
